    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>The mer of the Mermaid's Inn.</strong> Age unknown. CR 1/8. Amphibious: she breathes air and water.</p><p>She comes up the sea channel under the inn's floor most nights, dances in the great glass tank for coin and herring, and goes home to the reefs off the Sheldomar mouth before dawn. She likes Maud, dislikes noise and drunks, and sees everything that happens in the room through the glass. Nobody on land knows what she does with the coin.</p><p><strong>In the brawl</strong> she dives the moment the first table goes over, and the room loses its show. Afterwards, for a story or a fish, she will tell the party exactly who did what \u2014 including that the lady in grey went limp at precisely the right moment.</p><p><strong>She does not fight.</strong> If she must, she leaves by water, and no one follows her there.</p><p><em>Sheet derived from the Hennet Vole stat block (CR 0) \u2014 raised to CR 1/8 and 11 hp, swim 40 ft, walk 10 ft, Aquan added.</em></p>",
        "public": ""
      },
